// D2255 (plumb PL-025) — the `u8[][]` twin of `u8-list-literal`: the outer literal is a ref
// list whose inner literals only the destination can call packed byte lists.
//
// The PROOF reads an inner element, so a cell that built an i32 inner backing cannot print 200.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
[[1], [2, 200]]
// @@TYPE@@
u8[][]
// @@TEST@@
v.length == 2
// @@HIT@@
print(v[1][1])
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@WANT@@
200
// @@SKIP@@
return_inferred: an un-annotated function returns the literal at its own type, `i32[][]`, which is not a `u8[][]`
